{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_distributedpubsub", "label": "DistributedPubSub", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_distributedpubsubmediator", "label": "DistributedPubSubMediator", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One mediator per node at the well-known path /system/cluster/pubsub/mediator; subscribers register locally so the fan-out logic can assume locality."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_publish", "label": "Publish", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_subscribe", "label": "Subscribe", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Takes an optional replyTo because without it the answer follows context.sender, which is empty when tell is called outside an actor."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_unsubscribeall", "label": "UnsubscribeAll", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_subscriberejected", "label": "SubscribeRejected", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A Subscribe over a bound is rejected, not dropped, so the caller learns which limit refused it instead of seeing silence."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_anycast_one_subscriber_delivery", "label": "Anycast (one-subscriber delivery)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A stable rotation, not a draw: local subscribers in registration order then remote claimants sorted by address, so every mediator orders the remote half identically. A remote node counts as one candidate because the gossip frame carries topic names, not subscriber counts. A publishing node that also hosts workers rotates over two pointers, because a shared pointer would pin the originating pass to the local subscriber count and starve every remote candidate. Earns its place over a ClusterRouter only when the recipient set is dynamic."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_at_most_one_remote_hop", "label": "At-most-one-remote-hop fan-out", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One envelope per remote node, not per subscriber; an anycast whose far-side subscribers are already gone is NOT rerouted, because a second hop would trade the guarantee for a race with the gossip round that corrects the sender anyway."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_topic_to_node_gossip", "label": "Topic-to-node gossip", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deltas only ('node X now has/no longer has subscribers for topic Y'); lower gossipIntervalMs converges faster after subscribe/unsubscribe at the cost of more chatter."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_bounded_registries", "label": "Bounded PubSub registries", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "maxTopics and maxRemoteNodesPerTopic also apply to gossip: a peer announcing 100k topics used to create 100k entries on every receiving node without a single local Subscribe. Over-limit claims are dropped and logged but the connection stays, because a noisy peer should not cost a healthy connection."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_distributedpubsuboptions", "label": "DistributedPubSubOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_dead_letters_for_unrouted_publish", "label": "Dead letters for unrouted publishes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A typo'd topic name and a topic whose subscribers have not gossiped yet look identical from the publisher side; the dead letter is what tells them apart. A frame the mediator has no handler for at all (an older node reached by a newer wire kind) lands there too, with a warning, because a silently dropped frame looks exactly like an idle cluster."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_distributedpubsub", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_distributedpubsubmediator", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_distributedpubsubmediator", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_publish", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_distributedpubsubmediator", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_subscribe", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_distributedpubsubmediator", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_unsubscribeall", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_subscribe", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_subscriberejected", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_publish", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_anycast_one_subscriber_delivery", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_at_most_one_remote_hop", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_pubsub_publish", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_do